1. hit the base case, then climb back up and add what we have left that is 3, then again climb back up and add 2, where can it be added 2 at front the at back, then
again climb up and add 1 at each position using a loop


1,2,3 --> 2,3 --> 3 --> [] -->[3] --> [2,3],[3,2] --> [1,2,3] ,[2,1,3] ,[3,2,1]


#code 

```python

class Solution(object):
    def permute(self, nums):
        """
        :type nums: List[int]
        :rtype: List[List[int]]
        """
        
        if len(nums) == 0:
            return [[]]

        perms = self.permute(nums[1:])
        res = []
        for p in perms: #p in perms will be the array i.e [3] then [[2,3],[3,2]]
            for i in range(len(p)+1):
                p_copy = p.copy()
                p_copy.insert(i,nums[0])
                #append each nums[0] at every index len(p)+1 times here
                #becuz nums[0] will be the element which has to be added at
                #every index, like at first it will be 3 
                #then it will be 2 from 2,3 so 2 will be added before 3 and after 3
                #then at last level there will be 1 from 1,2,3 which will be added
                # in two permutes those are 2,3 and 3,2

                res.append(p_copy)
        return res

















